Spec: Scoped owned-runtime sharing

Purpose:
  Reuse a bounded authorized transport runtime across independent business flows without coupling their cancellation.

Owns:
  ./OwnedRuntimePool.java

Must:
  Share only exactly equal owner-provided scope keys, coalesce concurrent creation and count creating or closing resources against capacity.
  Hold a distinct lease per acquisition; closing one lease never closes a resource still leased by another flow.
  Create outside the pool lock and dispose a resource returned after shutdown, cancellation or invalidation before allowing its capacity slot to be reused.
  Bound waiter lifetime by its monotonic deadline without resetting another waiter's budget or starting duplicate creation.
  Close idle resources after the configured timeout and close all resources on failed current-authority/aliveness validation; keep maintenance external and threads bounded by the host.

  Allow a factory to register its resource before initialization; failed initialization retains cleanup ownership and its slot until close succeeds.
